cff-version: 1.2.0
title: An enzyme-resolved dataset linking drug interaction mechanisms to clinical severity grades
message: Cite this dataset version by its Zenodo DOI.
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23169653
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Noor
    given-names: Adeeb
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8251-1853
    affiliation: Department of Information Technology, Faculty of Computing and Information Technology, King Abdulaziz University, Jeddah, Saudi Arabia
abstract: >-
  Protein-attributed dataset of 1900 drug pairs, 240 drugs and 35 source
  protein labels. A deterministic transformation reconstructs primary record
  contents from deposited attribution and identifier snapshots; the original
  upstream subset selection remains unresolved. DDInter grades are reconstructed
  locally from the user's authorised download. A frozen human accession audit
  resolves two source symbol conflicts while preserving raw annotations.
  Includes exploratory statistics, descriptive author-archived reference
  membership comparisons, reported KEGG aggregates and a self-contained browser.
  Historical D3 rules and graph candidates provide partial source support.
  Clinical-trial flags and the incomplete phenotype layer are excluded.
keywords:
  - drug-drug interactions
  - cytochrome P450
  - drug transporters
  - DDInter
  - data provenance
repository-code: https://github.com/adeebnoor/ddi-enzyme-severity-resource
url: https://github.com/adeebnoor/ddi-enzyme-severity-resource
version: 2.3.0
date-released: 2026-10-05
